I am standing in the metro.
The train is very clean and cool.
I look at the map above the door.
There are many lines on the map.
I need to get near the sea.
But this train does not go there directly.
I need to change the train.
I do not understand the map.
An older woman is sitting near me.
I politely speak to her.
"Excuse me, aunty," I say.
She looks at me with a smile.
"I need to get near the sea," I say.
"At which station should I alight?"
Aunty looks at the map.
"You need to alight at the next junction," she says.
"From there, go by the blue line train," she tells me.
I understand the route now.
"Thank you, aunty," I happily say.
